# CF_ADAPTER: the 50-pin CompactFlash breadboard adapter (bought in). Its pins are the CF
# connector's, numbered as the card's, in True IDE mode (-ATA SEL, pin 9, grounded).
# Transcribed from SanDisk CompactFlash Product Manual 10.1, Table 3-1, "True IDE Mode Signal"
# (../datasheets/SanDisk CompactFlash Product Manual 10.1/). Active-low "-X" is written ~{X}.
# Types from the In/Out column: I input, O output, I/O bidirectional; ON = open drain
# (open_collector); OZ1 tri_state; "Ground" (grounded in the card) and "OPEN" passive.
#
# pin  name  type
1   GND        power_in
2   D03        bidirectional
3   D04        bidirectional
4   D05        bidirectional
5   D06        bidirectional
6   D07        bidirectional
7   ~{CS0}     input
8   A10        input
9   ~{ATA_SEL} input
10  A09        input
11  A08        input
12  A07        input
13  VCC        power_in
14  A06        input
15  A05        input
16  A04        input
17  A03        input
18  A02        input
19  A01        input
20  A00        input
21  D00        bidirectional
22  D01        bidirectional
23  D02        bidirectional
24  ~{IOCS16}  open_collector
25  ~{CD2}     passive
26  ~{CD1}     passive
27  D11        bidirectional
28  D12        bidirectional
29  D13        bidirectional
30  D14        bidirectional
31  D15        bidirectional
32  ~{CS1}     input
33  ~{VS1}     passive
34  ~{IORD}    input
35  ~{IOWR}    input
36  ~{WE}      input
37  INTRQ      tri_state
38  VCC        power_in
39  ~{CSEL}    input
40  ~{VS2}     passive
41  ~{RESET}   input
42  IORDY      open_collector
43  ~{INPACK}  tri_state
44  ~{REG}     input
45  ~{DASP}    open_collector
46  ~{PDIAG}   open_collector
47  D08        bidirectional
48  D09        bidirectional
49  D10        bidirectional
50  GND        power_in
